WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.940
Moviegoers can trust the "Transformers" franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:06.480
to deliver plenty of carnage on a&nbsp;
blockbuster scale, but the films&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.960
aren't exactly critical darlings. Will&nbsp;
"Rise of the Beasts" change all that?

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.580
"Transformers: Rise of the Beasts" features&nbsp;
a star-studded voice cast that includes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:19.140
Academy Award-winning Michelle Yeoh. The story&nbsp;
sees the titular shape-shifting robots team up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:23.280
with the Maximals for a pulse-pounding adventure.&nbsp;
But will the latest sequel fare better than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:27.120
previous flicks, or will it be dismissed&nbsp;
as just another loud, messy action movie?

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.020
The good news is that "Rise of the Beasts"&nbsp;
isn't the worst installment of the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.900
according to Rotten Tomatoes.&nbsp;
As of the making of this video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.340
the Steven Caple Jr.-directed actioner&nbsp;
is somewhere in the mid 60s to low 70s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.660
depending on when you see this, making it one of&nbsp;
the most well-received franchise outings to date.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.180
Owen Gleiberman of Variety praised the movie for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.360
being more grounded than previous&nbsp;
"Transformers" flicks, writing,

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.860
"It's got a relatable human story that works, and&nbsp;
thanks to a script that actually has sustained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.880
bursts of dialogue, the robots felt more real&nbsp;
to me as characters than they usually do."

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.520
"This is probably a lot for you, huh?"

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.140
At the same time, this is still a "Transformers"&nbsp;
movie, which means some reviews are guaranteed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.280
to be negative. The latest installment has&nbsp;
already garnered its fair share of detractors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:13.260
but the Rotten Tomatoes rating suggests that the&nbsp;
fans currently outweigh the naysayers. With that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.040
in mind, let's examine what the critics&nbsp;
are saying about "Rise of the Beasts."

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.940
The positive reviews of "Rise of the Beasts"&nbsp;
share the consensus that it's a fun time at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:24.780
the movies. Furthermore, unlike previous&nbsp;
films about the Autobots and Decepticons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:29.280
the franchise's seventh installment has plenty of&nbsp;
heart to complement the machine-driven carnage.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.880
Frank Scheck of the Hollywood Reporter&nbsp;
believes that "Rise of the Beasts" will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:36.840
entertain long-term fans, especially those&nbsp;
who grew up playing with the toys that paved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.140
the way for the movies, cartoons, video&nbsp;
games, and other media. Scheck wrote,

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:43.260
"These Hasbro action figures,&nbsp;
and their onscreen incarnations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:46.680
are capable of reducing even the&nbsp;
most mature, jaded adult into an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.440
awestruck child who just wants to get&nbsp;
down on the floor and play with them."

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:52.560
Elsewhere, ComicBook.com reviewer Liam Crowley was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.740
impressed with the action set pieces and&nbsp;
the film's entertainment value, writing,

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.980
"The action is pulse-pounding. The&nbsp;
summer movie season has been in full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.260
throttle for just over a month, and 'Transformers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:05.160
Rise of the Beasts' sends that popcorn&nbsp;
blockbuster momentum into full gear."

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:09.120
Steven Caple Jr.'s direction also received&nbsp;
some positive feedback from critics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:12.900
with Uproxx noting that he shows a genuine&nbsp;
affection for the characters that goes a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:17.760
long way. The reviewer also gave the movie props&nbsp;
for including some memorable '90s needle drops,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.680
so viewers can expect a banging soundtrack.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.880
While the positive reviews tease a heartfelt&nbsp;
action-adventure movie, some of the naysayers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:28.260
believe that "Rise of the Beasts" is unremarkable.&nbsp;
For example, Valerie Complex of Deadline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:31.860
praised the action sequences while arguing&nbsp;
that the story is nothing to write home about:

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:35.940
"'Rise of the Beasts' is another generic&nbsp;
story about an intergalactic menace from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.000
the sky that carries all the plot&nbsp;
predictability of a broken clock."

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.900
Indiewire reviewer Christian Zilker&nbsp;
offered a more scathing evaluation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:46.320
of the film, stating that it's&nbsp;
just another soulless blockbuster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.880
which is a bad look now that movies based&nbsp;
on toy brands are evolving. Zilker wrote,

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:55.920
"It's as if some executive saw Mattel and Greta&nbsp;
Gerwig turning 'Barbie' into genuine art, so they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.060
made a George Costanza-style decision to veer&nbsp;
in the opposite direction purely out of spite."

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:04.320
Charles Bramesco of the Guardian echoed these&nbsp;
sentiments and highlighted some issues with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:08.100
film's script, writing that the film might confuse&nbsp;
viewers who aren't familiar with the series:

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.160
"Everything has a vague partial&nbsp;
finish, as if director Steve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:15.120
Caple Jr and the five-person brain trust&nbsp;
responsible for the script banked on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:18.480
audience's familiarity with the shape of&nbsp;
a movie to fill in the gaps they've left."

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.500
Curious if "Rise of the Beasts" rises&nbsp;
above the franchise's less-than-stellar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:26.520
reputation? The latest "Transformers"&nbsp;
installment hits theaters on June 9th.

